PW=[
 {'id':'b2w1','part':1,'kind':'essay','t':'Deneme: Sosyal medya ve gençler','in':'In your English class you have been talking about technology. Now your English teacher has asked you to write an essay. Write your essay using all the notes and giving reasons for your point of view. Write 140–190 words.','mail':'Has social media done more harm than good for young people?\n\nNotes – write about:\n1. staying in touch with friends\n2. mental health\n3. ............ (your own idea)',
  'pts':WP(('Arkadaşlarla iletişimi tartış',['in touch','friends','contact','communicate','connect']),('Ruh sağlığını tartış',['mental health','anxiety','stress','self-esteem','depressed','compare']),('Kendi fikrini ekle',['also','another','in addition','moreover','furthermore']),('Sonuç / görüş',['in conclusion','to sum up','overall','on balance','in my opinion'])),'min':140,'max':190,
  'model':'Social media is now a central part of most teenagers\' lives, and opinions are divided about whether this is a positive development.\n\nOn the one hand, social media makes it easy to stay in touch with friends, even those who live far away. Young people can share experiences instantly and find others with similar interests, which can be especially valuable for those who feel isolated.\n\nOn the other hand, there is growing evidence that heavy use can damage mental health. Teenagers constantly compare themselves with the perfect images they see online, and this can lead to anxiety and low self-esteem.\n\nAnother important issue is the spread of false information. Many young people get their news from social media without checking whether it is reliable.\n\nOn balance, I believe social media is not harmful in itself; the problem is how it is used. If schools teach young people to use it critically and to limit their screen time, its benefits can outweigh its disadvantages.'},
 {'id':'b2w2','part':1,'kind':'essay','t':'Deneme: Turizm','in':'In your English class you have been talking about travel. Now your English teacher has asked you to write an essay. Write your essay using all the notes and giving reasons for your point of view. Write 140–190 words.','mail':'Is tourism good for the places that tourists visit?\n\nNotes – write about:\n1. jobs and money\n2. the environment\n3. ............ (your own idea)',
  'pts':WP(('İş ve gelirden bahset',['jobs','money','economy','income','employment']),('Çevreden bahset',['environment','pollution','rubbish','nature','damage']),('Kendi fikrini ekle',['also','another','in addition','moreover','culture','local people']),('Sonuç / görüş',['in conclusion','to sum up','overall','on balance','in my opinion'])),'min':140,'max':190,
  'model':'Tourism is one of the largest industries in the world, but its effects on popular destinations are not always positive.\n\nThe most obvious advantage is economic. Tourism creates jobs in hotels, restaurants and shops, and the money visitors spend can be used to improve roads, hospitals and schools. For many small towns, it is the main source of income.\n\nHowever, mass tourism can seriously damage the environment. Beaches become polluted, wildlife is disturbed and huge amounts of water and energy are used in areas where they are already scarce.\n\nIn addition, local people sometimes suffer. When too many apartments are rented to tourists, housing becomes too expensive for residents, and traditional neighbourhoods lose their character.\n\nIn conclusion, I believe tourism can be good for a place, but only if it is carefully managed. Limiting visitor numbers and investing tourist money in protecting nature would allow destinations to enjoy the benefits without destroying what makes them special.'},
 {'id':'b2w3','part':2,'kind':'article','t':'Makale: İdeal hafta sonu','in':'You see this announcement in an English-language magazine. Write your article in 140–190 words.','mail':'ARTICLES WANTED\nMy perfect weekend\nDescribe your idea of a perfect weekend. Where would you be? Who would you spend it with? What would you do?\nThe best articles will be published in our next issue.',
  'pts':WP(('Nerede olacağını anlat',['would be','in a','by the','at a','somewhere']),('Kiminle olacağını söyle',['with my','friends','family','alone','on my own']),('Ne yapacağını anlat',['would','start','spend','then','after that']),('Bir başlık kullan',['@title'])),'min':140,'max':190,
  'model':'Mountains, books and no phone signal\n\nAsk most people about their perfect weekend and they will talk about parties or shopping. Mine would be very different.\n\nI would spend it in a small wooden cabin in the mountains, ideally somewhere without a phone signal. The only people I would invite are my two closest friends, who share my love of walking and long conversations.\n\nOn Saturday, we would get up early and climb to the top of the nearest peak, taking a picnic with us. After lunch, we would lie in the grass and watch the clouds – something I never have time for during the week. In the evening, we would cook a simple meal on a fire and talk until midnight.\n\nSunday would be a lazy day. I would sleep late, read a good novel by the window and maybe go for a swim in a cold mountain lake.\n\nIt may not sound exciting, but for me, a weekend like this would be the best way to recharge before another busy week.'},
 {'id':'b2w4','part':2,'kind':'review','t':'İnceleme: Bir dizi','in':'You see this announcement on an English-language website. Write your review in 140–190 words.','mail':'REVIEWS WANTED\nA TV series worth watching\nHave you watched a TV series recently that you think others would enjoy? Write a review telling us what it is about, what you liked or disliked, and who you would recommend it to.',
  'pts':WP(('Konusunu anlat',['about','story','follows','plot','set in']),('Beğendiklerini / beğenmediklerini söyle',['liked','loved','enjoyed','however','disappointing','weak']),('Kime tavsiye ettiğini söyle',['recommend','anyone who','fans of','if you'])),'min':140,'max':190,
  'model':'A gripping mystery: The Lighthouse\n\nIf you are looking for something to watch on a long winter evening, The Lighthouse is an excellent choice.\n\nThe series is set on a small island off the coast of Scotland, where a young detective is sent to investigate the disappearance of a lighthouse keeper. As she talks to the island\'s few residents, she discovers that everyone seems to be hiding something.\n\nWhat I enjoyed most was the atmosphere. The wild landscapes and constant storms create a sense of isolation that keeps you on the edge of your seat. The acting is also superb, particularly the performance of the main character, who is both clever and vulnerable.\n\nMy only criticism is that the middle episodes are a little slow, and one or two storylines are never fully explained.\n\nOverall, I would highly recommend The Lighthouse to anyone who enjoys mysteries with complex characters. Just do not watch it alone at night!'},
 {'id':'b2w5','part':2,'kind':'email','t':'E-posta: Yaz işi tavsiyesi','in':'You have received this email from your English-speaking friend Chris. Write your email in 140–190 words.','mail':'From: Chris\nI\'m thinking of getting a summer job this year, but I\'m not sure what kind of job would suit me. You had a summer job last year, didn\'t you? What did you do, and what did you learn from it? What advice would you give me?\nThanks,\nChris',
  'pts':WP(('Ne iş yaptığını anlat',['worked','job','last summer','as a']),('Ne öğrendiğini söyle',['learned','learnt','taught me','realised']),('Tavsiye ver',['should','advice','recommend','if i were you','why don\'t you','make sure'])),'min':140,'max':190,
  'model':'Hi Chris,\nGreat to hear from you! Getting a summer job is a brilliant idea – I\'m sure you won\'t regret it.\n\nLast summer I worked as a waiter in a busy seaside restaurant. To be honest, the first week was a nightmare. I kept forgetting orders and once I dropped a whole tray of drinks! But I soon got the hang of it.\n\nThe job taught me a lot. I learned how to stay calm under pressure and how to deal with difficult customers politely. I also realised how important teamwork is – we only survived the busy evenings because we helped each other.\n\nAs for advice, I think you should choose a job where you meet lots of people, because you\'re so sociable. If I were you, I\'d start applying now, as the best jobs go quickly. And make sure you ask about the working hours before you accept anything – some places expect you to work very late.\n\nGood luck, and let me know what you decide!\nBest wishes,\nDeniz'}]

PS=[
 {'id':'b2s1','p':1,'t':'Part 1 · Tanışma: alışkanlıklar','ins':'Her soruya birkaç cümleyle, nedenler ve örnekler vererek cevap ver.','q':[
  ['How do you usually spend your evenings?',30,['usually','tend to','unless'],"I tend to spend most evenings at home studying, unless one of my friends suggests going out for a walk. On Fridays I usually watch a film with my family."],
  ['Do you prefer reading books or watching films? Why?',30,['I prefer','whereas','because'],"I prefer reading, because I can imagine the characters in my own way, whereas films sometimes disappoint me if they're different from what I expected."],
  ['What\'s something new you\'d like to learn in the future?',30,['I\'d love to','I\'ve always wanted','one day'],"I've always wanted to learn to sail. My uncle has a small boat, so I'm hoping he'll teach me next summer."],
  ['How important is it for you to have a routine?',30,['quite important','otherwise','I find that'],"Quite important, actually. I find that if I don't have a routine, I waste a lot of time and end up stressed before exams."]]},
 {'id':'b2s2','p':2,'t':'Part 2 · Fotoğraflar: öğrenme yolları','ins':'İki fotoğrafı 1 dakika karşılaştır ve soruyu cevapla.','img':[['👩‍🏫📚🧑‍🎓','Fotoğraf 1: Bir sınıfta öğretmen tahtada ders anlatıyor, öğrenciler not alıyor.'],['🧑‍💻🎧🏠','Fotoğraf 2: Bir genç evde kulaklıkla bilgisayardan çevrim içi ders izliyor.']],'q':[
  ['Your photographs show people learning in different ways. Compare the photographs, and say what the advantages of learning in each way might be.',60,['both photos','whereas','in contrast','might','I suppose','seems to'],"Both photos show people learning, but in different settings. In the first, there's a traditional classroom with a teacher explaining something at the board, whereas in the second a young man seems to be following an online lesson at home. One advantage of the classroom is that students can ask questions immediately and learn from each other. In contrast, learning online is much more flexible – the young man can probably choose when to study and watch the lesson again if he doesn't understand something. I suppose he also saves time travelling."],
  ['Which way of learning do you prefer? Why?',30,['I\'d go for','I prefer','because'],"I prefer the classroom, because I find it hard to concentrate on my own and I need someone to push me a bit."]]},
 {'id':'b2s3','p':2,'t':'Part 2 · Fotoğraflar: kutlamalar','ins':'İki fotoğrafı 1 dakika karşılaştır ve soruyu cevapla.','img':[['🎉🎂👨‍👩‍👧‍👦','Fotoğraf 1: Evde, kalabalık bir ailenin doğum günü kutlaması.'],['🎆🎶🏙️','Fotoğraf 2: Şehir meydanında havai fişekli büyük bir yılbaşı kutlaması.']],'q':[
  ['Your photographs show people celebrating in different ways. Compare the photographs, and say why the people might be celebrating like this.',60,['both','while','perhaps','might be','I imagine'],"Both photographs show people celebrating, but the atmosphere is quite different. The first one shows a family birthday party at home, with a cake and lots of relatives, while the second shows a huge crowd watching fireworks in a city square, probably on New Year's Eve. The family might be celebrating at home because it's more personal and they can spend time talking to each other. The people in the city, on the other hand, perhaps want to feel part of something bigger and enjoy the excitement of a crowd."],
  ['Which kind of celebration would you prefer? Why?',30,['I\'d rather','I prefer','because'],"I'd rather celebrate at home with my family, because big crowds make me a bit nervous and I prefer having real conversations."]]},
 {'id':'b2s4','p':3,'t':'Part 3 · Birlikte karar verme: Okul gezisi','ins':'Önce seçenekleri tartış (2 dakika), sonra karar ver (1 dakika).','opts':['🏛️ a history museum','🏭 a factory','🌲 a national park','🎭 a theatre','🔬 a science centre'],'q':[
  ['Imagine your school is planning a day trip for students. Here are some places they could visit. Talk about what students could learn from visiting these places.',120,['let\'s start with','what about','I think','that\'s true, but','students would learn'],"Let's start with the history museum. Students could learn about the past in a much more memorable way than from a textbook. A factory visit might seem boring, but it would show students how things are actually made and what kinds of jobs exist. The national park would be great for learning about nature and the environment, and students would also get some fresh air. A theatre trip could help students understand literature better. Finally, a science centre is usually very interactive, so students learn by doing experiments themselves."],
  ['Now decide which place would be the best for a school trip.',60,['I think we should','the best option','because','although'],"I think the best option would be the science centre, because it's both educational and fun, and students of all ages would enjoy it, although the national park would be my second choice."]]},
 {'id':'b2s5','p':4,'t':'Part 4 · Tartışma: eğitim','ins':'Görüşünü nedenler ve örneklerle açıkla.','q':[
  ['Do you think students learn more outside the classroom than inside it?',45,['in some ways','however','for instance','I\'d argue'],"In some ways, yes. For instance, you learn teamwork from sport and responsibility from part-time jobs. However, I'd argue that the classroom is still essential for building basic knowledge."],
  ['Should school days be shorter so that students have more free time?',45,['I\'m not convinced','on the one hand','on the other hand'],"I'm not convinced. On the one hand, students would be less tired. On the other hand, they might just spend the extra time on their phones rather than doing something useful."],
  ['How might education change in the next twenty years?',45,['I imagine','is likely to','will probably','might'],"I imagine technology is likely to play a much bigger role. Lessons will probably be more personalised, with programs adapting to each student's level. But I think teachers will still be needed to motivate students."]]}]

